    "title": "Angela Dugalić named UCLA Student-Athlete of the Week after standout basketball performance - West LA Times",
    "text": "Graduate student Angela Dugalić has been named the UCLA Student-Athlete of the Week for her performance in athletic competitions from November 18 to 24. Dugalić, a forward for the UCLA Women’s Basketball team, scored a season-high 20 points during No. 3 UCLA’s 88-37 victory over Southern University on Sunday. She made three out of six attempts from three-point range, shot eight-for-fifteen overall, and collected five rebounds. The Des Plaines, Illinois native has reached double-digit scoring in four consecutive games.\nDugalić is currently averaging career highs with 11.3 points and seven rebounds per game over her first six appearances this season. She is shooting 50.9 percent from the field and 40 percent from beyond the arc.\nThis recognition marks Dugalić’s first time receiving the UCLA Student-Athlete of the Week award.\nOther nominees for this week’s honor included Skyy Clark (men’s basketball), Emma Egizii (women’s soccer), and Lola Schumacher (women’s volleyball).\nThe list of previous winners includes Bella Winn, Daphne Nakfoor, Bode Brinkema, Ryder Dodd, Eliana Urzua, Nico Iamaleava, Jalen Berger, Anthony Frias II, Sergi Solans Ormo, Gianna Kneepkens among others.",
